  "prefLabel": "He-P 1608.06 Notification of Work",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 1608.06 Notification of Work.\n\n(a) The lead abatement contractor or person granted a variance in accordance with He-P 1605.03, shall notify the department electronically through the lead on-line portal at https://nh-dhhs.my.site.com/lead/s/ or via email to nhleadprogram@dhhs.nh.gov of the intended schedule of work at least 5 days before lead abatement work begins.\n\n(b) A complete notification of work shall be submitted to the department and the owner or owner’s agent at least 5 days prior to the abatement project beginning and include:\n\n(1) The date when lead-based paint activities will start;\n\n(2) The date when lead-based paint activities will end, approximation using best professional judgement;\n\n(3) The lead abatement contractor business name and license number;\n\n(4) Contact information for the lead abatement contractor’s business including name, phone number, and email for the primary contact person;\n\n(5) The property address for abatement work including apartment or unit number(s), if applicable; and\n\n(6) The name and license number for the lead abatement supervisor for the project.\n\n(c) If not received by the department prior, a notification of work shall be accompanied by:\n\n(1) A copy of the work scope, detailing actions to be taken to abate or manage by interim controls all lead-based substances; and\n\n(2) A copy of the occupant protection plan prepared in accordance with He-P 1608.05.\n\n(d) Notification of changes to the start or end date(s) documented on the notification of work shall be made by the lead abatement contractor, lead abatement supervisor, or person granted a variance by notifying the department through the lead on-line portal at https://nh-dhhs.my.site.com/lead/s/, via email to nhleadprogram@dhhs.nh.gov, or by contacting the department by telephone at least 48 hours before the new start or end date(s).\n\n(e) The owner or owner’s agent of a leased or rented dwelling or dwelling unit shall provide written notification to all occupants affected by the lead hazard reduction work at least 5 days in advance of the proposed lead hazard reduction work, which includes:\n\n(1) Scheduled dates and work hours for the lead hazard reduction work;\n\n(2) Identification of work site(s);\n\n(3) Information on the alternative entrance or exit to be used during the work; and\n\n(4) A copy of the occupant protection plan.\n\nSource. #5920, eff 1-1-95; amd by #6096, eff 9-22-95; ss by #7181, eff 12-24-99; ss by #7495, eff 5-23-01; ss by #8039, eff 2-13-04; ss by #8932, eff 7-6-07; ss by #9986, eff 9-1-11, EXPIRED: 9-1-19 (from He-P 1605.05)\n\nNew. #13052, eff 6-11-20; ss by #14230, eff 4-2-25; ss by #14680, eff 8-26-26, EXPIRES: 8-26-36",
